{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774134818,"nonce":"hGHHqZLqg+5G78o2dKg1k8kGXos=","title":"P3: Graph node hover actions with overflow menu","message":"## What\n\nAdd hover action buttons to graph nodes — a small floating toolbar that appears when the user hovers over a node. Primary actions are always visible; secondary actions live in a three-dot overflow menu. This matches the pattern used in GitHub (PR review comments), Slack (message hover actions), etc.\n\n## Motivation\n\nCurrently, clicking a graph node navigates to its detail view (issues tab, sessions tab, auth tab). This is the only interaction available. Users need quick access to common operations (copy ID, view info, resume work) without leaving the graph. The hover action bar provides this without cluttering the canvas.\n\n## Design\n\n### Hover Action Bar Layout\n\n```\n  ┌─────────────────────────┐\n  │ [Copy] [Navigate] [···] │   ← appears above/below the node on hover\n  └─────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n- **Position**: Floats above the hovered node (below if near top edge of viewport). Rendered as HTML `position: fixed` div (like the existing GraphTooltip), NOT as SVG — this allows standard button styles, focus management, and overflow menus.\n- **Timing**: Appears after a short delay (~200ms hover dwell) to avoid flickering during casual mouse movement. Disappears when the mouse leaves both the node AND the action bar (with a ~150ms grace period for the gap between node and bar).\n- **Replaces tooltip on hover**: When the action bar is visible, the existing tooltip is suppressed (they occupy the same space conceptually). The action bar includes a condensed node label/type as header text.\n- **Persistence**: The action bar stays open while the mouse is over it (even if it leaves the node shape). It closes on mouse-out from the bar area, on Escape key, or on any action execution.\n\n### Primary Buttons (always visible on hover)\n\n| Button | Icon | All node types | Behavior |\n|--------|------|---------------|----------|\n| **Copy** | clipboard icon | Yes | Copies node ID to clipboard (issue human ID, session ID, auth request ID). Toast confirmation. |\n| **Go to** | arrow-right / external-link icon | Yes | Navigates to the node's detail view — same as current click behavior (`onNavigate`). |\n\n### Overflow Menu (three-dot button)\n\nClicking the three-dot button opens a dropdown menu below/above the button. The menu items vary by node type:\n\n#### Issue nodes\n| Action | Behavior |\n|--------|----------|\n| **Copy ID** | Copy issue human ID (redundant with primary Copy, but included for discoverability) |\n| **Resume Work** | Calls `spawnIssueAgent(repoId, issueId)` — spawns a new SDK session to continue work on this issue. Only shown if the issue has status `open`. |\n| **View in Issues tab** | Navigate to `#/issues?repo=...\u0026issue=...` |\n| **Copy branch** | Copy the `node.branch` value if present |\n\n#### Session nodes\n| Action | Behavior |\n|--------|----------|\n| **Copy session ID** | Copy full session ID |\n| **View conversation** | Navigate to `#/chat-history?session=...` |\n| **View in Sessions tab** | Navigate to `#/sessions?session=...` |\n| **Copy branch** | Copy `node.branch` if present |\n\n#### Auth request nodes\n| Action | Behavior |\n|--------|----------|\n| **Copy request ID** | Copy auth request ID |\n| **View in Auth tab** | Navigate to `#/auth?request=...` |\n\n### Interaction with existing click behavior\n\nCurrent behavior: clicking a node calls `onNavigate` (navigates to detail view). With P3:\n- **Click on the node shape** still calls `onNavigate` (unchanged).\n- **Hover** shows the action bar (new).\n- The action bar's \"Go to\" button duplicates the click behavior, providing an explicit affordance for the same action. This is intentional — some users prefer explicit buttons over implicit click targets.\n\n### Interaction with drag\n\nIf the user starts dragging a node (mousedown + mousemove, which D3 drag behavior would handle), the action bar should be dismissed immediately and not reappear until the drag ends and a new hover dwell period completes.\n\n## Implementation\n\n### New files\n\n- `ui/src/components/graph/HoverActionBar.tsx` (~150 lines) — the hover action bar component\n- `ui/src/components/graph/OverflowMenu.tsx` (~80 lines) — the three-dot dropdown menu\n\n### Modified files\n\n- `ui/src/components/graph/GraphCanvas.tsx` — add hover dwell tracking, render HoverActionBar, suppress tooltip when action bar visible\n- `ui/src/components/graph/index.ts` — export new components\n- `ui/src/style.css` — add hover action bar and overflow menu styles (~80 lines)\n- `ui/src/types/graph.ts` — potentially add action callback types to GraphCanvasProps\n\n### HoverActionBar props\n\n```typescript\ninterface HoverActionBarProps {\n  node: SimGraphNode\n  x: number          // screen X (center of node, transformed by zoom)\n  y: number          // screen Y (top of node, transformed by zoom)\n  onCopy: (text: string) =\u003e void\n  onNavigate: (type: GraphNodeType, id: string, repoId?: string) =\u003e void\n  onSpawnAgent?: (repoId: string, issueId: string) =\u003e Promise\u003cvoid\u003e\n  onDismiss: () =\u003e void\n}\n```\n\n### Hover state machine in GraphCanvas\n\n```\nIDLE → (mouseenter node, start 200ms timer) → DWELL_WAIT\nDWELL_WAIT → (timer fires) → ACTION_BAR_VISIBLE\nDWELL_WAIT → (mouseleave node) → IDLE\nACTION_BAR_VISIBLE → (mouseleave node AND bar, start 150ms timer) → GRACE_PERIOD\nACTION_BAR_VISIBLE → (mouseenter bar) → ACTION_BAR_VISIBLE (stay)\nGRACE_PERIOD → (mouseenter node or bar) → ACTION_BAR_VISIBLE\nGRACE_PERIOD → (timer fires) → IDLE\nACTION_BAR_VISIBLE → (action executed) → IDLE\nACTION_BAR_VISIBLE → (Escape key) → IDLE\nACTION_BAR_VISIBLE → (drag start) → IDLE\n```\n\nThis state machine lives in GraphCanvas as a `useReducer` or a set of refs (refs preferred since it interacts with D3 event handlers that are not Preact-managed).\n\n### Screen position calculation\n\nThe action bar needs screen-space coordinates, not simulation-space. To convert:\n1. Read the node's simulation `(x, y)` from `nodesRef`\n2. Apply the current zoom transform: `transform.apply([x, y])` → `[screenX, screenY]`\n3. Offset relative to the SVG container's bounding rect (containerRef.getBoundingClientRect())\n4. Position the bar above the node: `top = containerScreenY + screenY - barHeight - nodeRadius - 8`\n\n### Overflow menu\n\nThe OverflowMenu renders as a `position: absolute` dropdown anchored to the three-dot button. It uses a portal or just nests inside the action bar div. Click outside dismisses it.\n\nMenu items are passed as an array:\n```typescript\ninterface OverflowMenuItem {\n  label: string\n  onClick: () =\u003e void\n  disabled?: boolean\n}\n```\n\n### CSS\n\n```css\n.graph-hover-bar { ... }           /* container: flex row, rounded, dark bg, shadow */\n.graph-hover-bar__btn { ... }      /* icon button: 28x28, hover highlight */\n.graph-hover-bar__label { ... }    /* condensed node label text */\n.graph-hover-bar__sep { ... }      /* thin vertical separator */\n.graph-overflow { ... }            /* dropdown menu container */\n.graph-overflow__item { ... }      /* menu item row */\n.graph-overflow__item:hover { ... }\n.graph-overflow__item--disabled { ... }\n```\n\nStyle: dark background matching `--bg-card`, subtle border, `box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft)`, border-radius 8px. Buttons are icon-only with title attributes for accessibility. The overflow dropdown has the same background/border treatment.\n\n### Accessibility\n\n- Action bar buttons have `title` and `aria-label` attributes\n- Overflow menu items are `\u003cbutton\u003e` elements (not `\u003ca\u003e` or `\u003cdiv\u003e`)\n- Escape closes the action bar and overflow menu\n- Tab key moves focus between action bar buttons (natural browser behavior since they are real HTML buttons)\n\n## Edge cases\n\n- **Zoomed out far**: If the node is very small on screen, the action bar may be disproportionately large. Acceptable — the bar is a fixed size regardless of zoom. This matches how GitHub's hover actions work (fixed UI size over variable content).\n- **Node near canvas edge**: Clamp the action bar position to stay within the container bounds, similar to existing tooltip clamping.\n- **Rapid hover between nodes**: The 200ms dwell timer resets when moving to a different node. Only one action bar visible at a time.\n- **Overflow menu open + mouseleave**: If the overflow menu is open, the grace period timer does NOT start until the overflow menu is also left. The overflow menu keeps the action bar alive.\n- **Mobile/touch**: Not a target for P3. Touch users can still use click-to-navigate.\n\n## Estimated lines\n\n| File | Lines (est.) |\n|------|-------------|\n| `HoverActionBar.tsx` | 150 |\n| `OverflowMenu.tsx` | 80 |\n| `GraphCanvas.tsx` changes | 60 |\n| `style.css` additions | 80 |\n| Minor changes (index.ts, types) | 10 |\n| **Total** | **~380** |\n\n## Implementation order\n\n1. Add CSS classes for hover bar and overflow menu\n2. Implement `OverflowMenu.tsx` (standalone, testable)\n3. Implement `HoverActionBar.tsx` (depends on OverflowMenu)\n4. Wire hover state machine into `GraphCanvas.tsx`\n5. Connect `onSpawnAgent` to `spawnIssueAgent` from api.ts (plumbed through GraphView)\n6. Build and verify","files":null}]}